I fell down the stairs and my knees are quite blue.

35
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:06,800
Oh no, see?

36
00:02:07,560 --> 00:02:08,740
High heels are dangerous.

37
00:02:09,140 --> 00:02:10,780
I don't know why women wear them.

38
00:02:10,780 --> 00:02:14,140
Well, I don't know, but that's not what we're here to discover.

39
00:02:14,620 --> 00:02:14,740
Right.

40
00:02:15,620 --> 00:02:21,240
Okay, so let's take a look at some of these great phrases in Fluency Builder.

41
00:02:26,760 --> 00:02:33,100
I really liked how this receptionist used some excellent phrases to sound really professional.

42
00:02:34,540 --> 00:02:36,900
One thing she said was, certainly.

43
00:02:38,310 --> 00:02:38,890
Certainly.

44
00:02:39,340 --> 00:02:39,570
Certainly.

45
00:02:40,620 --> 00:02:41,910
So why did she say certainly?

46
00:02:42,660 --> 00:02:50,630
Well this is a nice way to respond, to make the other person know that you understand what they said.

47
00:02:51,160 --> 00:02:55,490
So Josh O'Neil said, yes, I'm here to see you Joanna Stevens.

48
00:02:56,230 --> 00:02:57,430
I have an appointment at four.

49
00:02:57,870 --> 00:02:58,250
Certainly.

50
00:02:58,790 --> 00:03:00,990
So she is saying, I understand what you said.

51
00:03:01,510 --> 00:03:01,630
Yes.

52
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:04,580
So she said, may I take your name?

53
00:03:04,580 --> 00:03:05,550
May I take your name?

54
00:03:06,140 --> 00:03:07,670
May I take your name?

55
00:03:08,100 --> 00:03:11,610
So this is a nice way of saying, what is your name?

56
00:03:12,220 --> 00:03:13,220
Yeah.

57
00:03:13,220 --> 00:03:17,630
So, now this is really important because if you said, what is your name?

58
00:03:18,020 --> 00:03:18,310
Is that correct?

59
00:03:18,750 --> 00:03:21,450
It's correct, but it's not really very...

60
00:03:22,260 --> 00:03:22,550
Exactly.

61
00:03:23,260 --> 00:03:25,570
Or I would say polite to a certain extent.

62
00:03:26,100 --> 00:03:27,100
Yes.

63
00:03:27,100 --> 00:03:28,100
Okay.

64
00:03:28,100 --> 00:03:29,100
So may I take your name?

65
00:03:29,100 --> 00:03:29,510
May I take your name?

66
00:03:30,100 --> 00:03:35,380
So you use this phrase when you are going to write down the person's name.

67
00:03:35,380 --> 00:03:36,380
Right.

68
00:03:36,380 --> 00:03:41,580
So if you meet somebody on the street or at a bar, you wouldn't say, may I take your name?

69
00:03:42,060 --> 00:03:43,060
No.

70
00:03:43,060 --> 00:03:44,060
Right.

71
00:03:44,060 --> 00:03:45,620
Unless you're going to write it down.

72
00:03:45,620 --> 00:03:49,940
So usually for an office setting where the receptionist has to write down the name.

73
00:03:50,340 --> 00:03:51,340
Yes.

74
00:03:51,340 --> 00:03:53,100
Alright, one more phrase.

75
00:03:53,100 --> 00:03:55,900
Ms. Stevens will be with you momentarily.

76
00:03:56,160 --> 00:03:56,480
Okay.

77
00:03:56,900 --> 00:04:01,340
So, Ms. Stevens will be with you momentarily.

78
00:04:01,340 --> 00:04:02,400
